  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that $C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(C).$",
  "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(8-18)\\cdot (36-10) \\\\  & =(-10)\\cdot 26 \\\\  & =-260.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
